  "label": "Computational Protein And Ligand Design",
  "related": [
    "resistance-analysing-antifungal-a8e9",
    "application-glycomics-glycomics-01d4",
    "engineering-stability-63ff"
  ],
  "secondary_categories": [],
  "slug": "aeruginosa-pseudomonas-aeruginosa-37ae",
  "summary": "Learned generative models are now paired with structure prediction, docking, and MD to validate designed binders, antibodies, and enzymes.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is generative or search-based design of proteins and ligands, tightly coupled to structure prediction, docking, affinity estimation, or molecular dynamics validation. Preprints report miniprotein and binder workflows: BindCraft yields 42/50 IL-23 p19 designs above ipSAE 0.60, and epitope excision cuts RFdiffusion and AlphaFold3 GPU time by about 88%. UnibindMD chains BindCraft design with AlphaFold3 or Boltz-2 prediction, PRODIGY affinity, ADMET-AI profiling, and 100 ns MD. Pythia-1 designs full-length IgG antibodies against 22 targets, including GPCR agonists and antagonists. Published work applies reinforcement learning and mixture-of-experts frameworks to antibody and enzyme optimization, and physics-based pose prediction is evaluated in an antiviral blind challenge. The novelty is methodological integration of generative design with computational validation rather than a single shared result.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-10-28"
}
